comments.text:
/-!
# Standing waves, the master clock and the harmonic map

**Standing waves.**  On any finite abelian node group `G` (the torus `ZMod N × ZMod M`, the
hypercube, a cycle), the standing wave made from a signal `f` at time-offset `a` is the sum of the
wave moved forward and the wave moved backward, `x ↦ f (x + a) + f (x - a)`.

* `spec_standing` — in the mode picture every mode `ψ` is multiplied by `ψ a + ψ (-a)`;
* `standing_factor_eq` — that factor is the *real* number `2 Re (ψ a)`, so the modes of a standing
  wave do not turn: they only breathe (`standing_phase_locked`);
* `standing_node` — modes where the factor vanishes are silent at that time (nodes);
* `standing_time_reversal` — the standing wave is the same for `a` and `-a`;
* `standing_power` — the power of each mode is scaled by `|ψ a + ψ(-a)|²`.

**The master clock.**  Several components ticking together (torus flow, merkaba turns, braid
steps) form one system whose state is the tuple of their states.

* `joint_period` — the period of the joint system is the least common multiple of the periods;
* `joint_return_iff` — the joint state returns exactly at common multiples of the periods;
* `joint_orderOf` — the same for group elements: `orderOf (a, b) = lcm (orderOf a) (orderOf b)`.

**The harmonic map.**  A value `v` (for example a letter's number) is sent to the torus mode
`(v mod N, v mod M)`.

* `harmonicMap_bijective` — if `N` and `M` are coprime, this map from `ZMod (N * M)` to the torus
  `ZMod N × ZMod M` is a bijection: every value up to `N M` gets its own node, and it preserves
  sums and products (`harmonicMap_add`, `harmonicMap_mul`);
* `harmonicMap_not_injective` — if they are not coprime, two different values share a node.
-/

