/-!
# The Kauffman bracket is the quantum trace

* `localMat_sl2R`, `localMat_sl2RInv`: the skein relations `Ř = q·1 − E`, `Ř⁻¹ = q⁻¹·1 − E` of the
  `U_q(sl₂)` R-matrix, `E` the Temperley–Lieb generator `tlE`;
* `bracketAux`: Python's Temperley–Lieb state recursion for `kauffman_bracket`, over any
  commutative ring (`map_bracketAux`: it commutes with ring homomorphisms);
* `repMat_eq_kaufW`: with `q = −A²`, `ρ(B) = (−A)^w · ∏ (A^{±1}·1 + A^{∓1}·E)`;
* `qTrace_phi_kaufW`: expanding the product diagram by diagram gives the recursion;
* `quantumTrace_eq_bracket`: `Tr(μ^{⊗ n} ρ(B)) = (−A)^w · (−A² − A⁻²) · ⟨B̂⟩`.
-/

