/-!
# Exponent windows of integer Laurent polynomials

Auxiliary facts for the Burau certificates (`BraidBurauCert.lean`):

* `InWin lo hi f`: every non-zero coefficient of `f ∈ ℤ[t, t⁻¹]` has exponent in `[lo, hi]`;
  closed under sums, products (windows add), finite sums and products, determinants;
* `eq_sum_of_inWin`: such an `f` is `∑_{k < hi - lo + 1} f(lo + k) t^{lo + k}`;
* `eq_of_evalAt_eq`: two Laurent polynomials in a common window `[lo, hi]` that agree at
  more than `hi - lo` distinct non-zero rationals are equal — exact equality of Laurent
  polynomials can be decided by computing in `ℚ`;
* `detLap`: the determinant by expansion along the first row (computable by the kernel),
  equal to `Matrix.det`.
-/

/-- **Four-point condition.** For all `a b c e`, each of the three pair-sums
`d a b + d c e`, `d a c + d b e`, `d a e + d b c` is at most the maximum of the other two;
equivalently, the largest value is attained (at least) twice. -/

