/-!
# The unique longest element of `W(Bₙ)`, for every `n`

`WeylLongestBFG.lean` treats `B₃`, `B₄`, `B₅` with explicit root lists.  Here `n = L + 1` is
arbitrary.  The positive roots are given as a family, through the usual signed-permutation model:

* `bnCartan n`: the Cartan matrix of `Bₙ` in simple-root coordinates, with the short simple root
  last (`C (n-1) (n-2) = -2`); `bn_isCartanFor`: it realises Mathlib's `CoxeterMatrix.Bₙ n`
  (by the rank-two reduction `isCartanFor_of_local`);
* `prefixT n x k = x₀ + ⋯ + x_k`: the simple-root coordinates of the vector `∑ xⱼ εⱼ`, for the
  simple roots `αₖ = εₖ - εₖ₊₁` (`k < n - 1`) and `α_{n-1} = ε_{n-1}`;
* `bnSigma n i`: the action of `sᵢ` on `ε`-coordinates (swap `i ↔ i + 1`, or change the sign of
  coordinate `n - 1`); **`cRefl_prefixT`**: `sᵢ (prefixT x) = prefixT (bnSigma i x)`;
* `bnPos n`: the positive roots `εₐ -ε_b` (`a < b`), `εₐ + ε_b` (`a > b`), `εₐ`, indexed by
  `Fin n × Fin n`; `bnPos_isPositiveRootSet`;
* `bnCrep_w0`: the image `w₀` of the Garside element `Δ = c^n` of `ArtinBn` (`bnDelta`) acts as
  `-1` (the Coxeter element acts on `ε`-coordinates by `x ↦ (x₁, …, x_{n-1}, -x₀)`);
* `bnPos_card`: there are `n²` positive roots;
* **`bn_length_eq_sq_iff`**: `ℓ(w) = n²` iff `w = w₀` (`bn_length_eq_iff` with `|bnPos n|`);
  `bn_length_le_sq`: `ℓ(w) ≤ n²`; `bnCrep_injective`: the reflection representation is faithful.

No `sorry`, no `native_decide`; nothing is checked by finite computation.
-/

