comments.text:
/-!
# `TorusBraidGroup` is Bellingeri's Theorem 1.2 at genus 1 (D3 source check; registry H-119)

This file checks the D3 presentation of `B_n(T²)` (`torusRels`, `TorusBraid.lean`) against its
source: P. Bellingeri, *On presentations of surface braid groups*, J. Algebra 274 (2004);
arXiv:math/0110129v2 (copy in `QBX/docs/reference/`).

`closedRels g n` writes down the presentation of **Theorem 1.2** (closed orientable surface of
genus `g ≥ 1`, `n` strands) for every genus `g`, line by line as printed, with all handle indices
`r, s` and the far-commutation condition `|i − j| ≥ 2` kept as in the paper:

* generators `σ_1, …, σ_{n-1}, a_1, …, a_g, b_1, …, b_g` (`BGen g n`, everything 0-indexed);
* braid relations `σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i = σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}`, `σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i` (`|i − j| ≥ 2`);
* (R1) `a_r σ_i = σ_i a_r`, `b_r σ_i = σ_i b_r` (`i ≠ 1`);
* (R2) `σ_1⁻¹ a_r σ_1⁻¹ a_r = a_r σ_1⁻¹ a_r σ_1⁻¹`, and the same for `b_r`;
* (R3) for `s < r`: `σ_1⁻¹ a_s σ_1 a_r = a_r σ_1⁻¹ a_s σ_1`, `σ_1⁻¹ b_s σ_1 b_r = b_r σ_1⁻¹ b_s σ_1`,
  `σ_1⁻¹ a_s σ_1 b_r = b_r σ_1⁻¹ a_s σ_1`, `σ_1⁻¹ b_s σ_1 a_r = a_r σ_1⁻¹ b_s σ_1`;
* (R4) `σ_1⁻¹ a_r σ_1⁻¹ b_r = b_r σ_1⁻¹ a_r σ_1`;
* (TR) `[a_1, b_1⁻¹] ⋯ [a_g, b_g⁻¹] = σ_1 σ_2 ⋯ σ_{n-1}² ⋯ σ_2 σ_1`, with `[x, y] = x y x⁻¹ y⁻¹`.

Relations that mention `σ_1` are only imposed when `σ_1` exists (`n ≥ 2`).

Main result: `torusBraidEquivBellingeri : TorusBraidGroup n ≃* PresentedGroup (closedRels 1 n)`,
sending `σ_i ↦ σ_i`, `a ↦ a_1`, `b ↦ b_1`. So the D3 presentation is exactly the genus-1 case of
Theorem 1.2. (That Theorem 1.2 presents `π₁` of the configuration space is the paper's result and
is not proved here.)
-/

