comments.text:
/-!
# Hyperbolic gyrovector spaces and the Lorentz model of deep embeddings

Entry point importing the whole development:

* `Gyrogroup`       — abstract gyrogroups / gyrovector spaces (Ungar's axioms) and their
                       elementary theory;
* `MobiusAdd`       — Möbius addition on the unit ball of a real inner product space;
* `Gyration`        — Möbius gyrations, gyrator identity, gyroassociativity, left loop,
                       gyrocommutativity;
* `MobiusScalar`    — Möbius scalar multiplication and the gyrovector space axioms;
* `PoincareBall`    — the Poincaré ball as a gyrocommutative gyrogroup and gyrovector space;
* `PoincareMetric`  — the Poincaré gyrodistance, its `cosh` formula, metric space structure,
                       isometries;
* `HyperbolicNN`    — exp/log maps, Möbius matrix–vector multiplication, hyperbolic layers;
* `Curvature`       — all of the above in curvature `-c`;
* `Lorentz`         — the hyperboloid (Lorentz) model, its distance, the isometry with the
                       Poincaré ball, tangent spaces, exp/log maps;
* `Geodesic`        — gyrolines are constant-speed geodesics, gyromidpoints;
* `Klein`           — the Beltrami–Klein model, isometric to the Poincaré ball and the
                       hyperboloid;
* `Einstein`        — Einstein addition, isomorphic to Möbius addition; the Klein ball as a
                       gyrocommutative gyrogroup;
* `LorentzCentroid` — squared Lorentzian distance and its closed-form centroid (unique
                       minimiser of the weighted sum of squared distances);
* `ParallelTransport` — parallel transport in the Poincaré ball (via gyrations) and in the
                       Lorentz model; both are isometries of the tangent spaces;
* `EinsteinMidpoint` — the weighted Einstein midpoint on the Klein ball, equal to the
                       projection of the Lorentzian centroid;
* `LorentzHyperplane` — the distance from a point to a Lorentz hyperplane,
                       `arsinh |⟨n, p⟩_L|` (hyperbolic multinomial logistic regression).
-/

