/-- **Homology of formal proof DAGs.**
1. a well-formed proof DAG (every node refers only to earlier nodes) contains no circular
   reasoning;
2. in every dependency graph, circular reasoning forces `b₁ ≥ 1`, so `b₁ = 0` excludes it;
3. the derivation complex of every cut-free proof tree has `H₀ ≅ ℤ`, `H_k = 0` for `k ≥ 1` and
   `b₁ = 0`;
4. cut elimination of a closed proof with cuts proving `φ` yields a cut-free tree proving `φ`,
   with isomorphic integral homology in every degree;
5. every formula accepted by the DAG verifier on a well-formed DAG is valid (for every notion
   of validity for which the rules are sound), by transfinite induction over the autonomously
   constructed ordinal ranking. -/

