/-!
# Sensor-grid reconstruction of `C²` fields: the `δ² ‖∇²Φ‖` bound

A sensor array with discretisation scale `δ > 0` samples a field `Φ : ℝⁿ → V` (with values
in any real normed space `V`) on the lattice `δ ℤⁿ`.  From these samples alone we reconstruct
a continuous field by **multilinear interpolation**: interpolate linearly in coordinate
`0`, then in coordinate `1`, …, then in coordinate `n - 1`.

Main results:

* `interp_error_1d`: the one-dimensional estimate
  `‖g(x) - ((1-θ) g(a) + θ g(b))‖ ≤ M/2 · θ(1-θ) (b-a)²` for `‖g''‖ ≤ M`;
* `interpCoord_error`: linear interpolation in one coordinate at scale `δ` has error at most
  `δ² M / 8` if `‖∇²Φ‖ ≤ M`;
* `interpAll_error`: the full multilinear interpolant has error at most `n δ² M / 8`;
* `multilinearInterp_congr_grid`: the multilinear interpolant only depends on the grid samples;
* `reconstruct` and `reconstruct_sample`: the reconstruction from raw samples
  `(Fin n → ℤ) → V`, which agrees with the interpolant of every field having those samples;
* `reconstruct_sample_error`: `‖Φ x - reconstruct δ (sample δ Φ) x‖ ≤ n δ² M / 8`;
* `reconstruct_grid`: the reconstruction reproduces the samples exactly on the grid.
-/

