comments.text:
/-- **Monotonic compression theorem.** Iterating meta-inductive compression with arbitrary,
round-dependent, untrusted rewriters, starting from a well-formed library `L₀`:
1. the sequents never change (no loss of deductive power), and the invariant is kept;
2. the total Kolmogorov certificate size is antitone;
3. at each round the library is either unchanged or its size strictly decreases;
4. at most `libSize L₀` rounds are strict;
5. the compression ratio is antitone and at most `1`;
6. every lemma's certificate size bounds the Kolmogorov complexity of its conclusion relative
   to the proof-checking decoder. -/

